  m_Name: LS UV LatLong
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_functionInfo: "// Made with Amplify Shader Editor v1.9.9.5\n// Available at the
    Unity Asset Store - http://u3d.as/y3X \n/*ASEBEGIN\nVersion=19905\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;373;129.0405,2384;Inherit;False;2818.831;1331.493;Math;46;438;434;468;444;437;436;435;432;433;467;463;462;458;457;461;460;459;456;455;454;453;452;451;450;449;448;447;446;445;443;442;441;431;430;429;428;427;426;425;424;423;400;409;407;402;406;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;372;128,1952;Inherit;False;775.6106;382.3025;UV
    Lat Long Node - Amplify Shader Pack Example;2;278;399;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;482;128,3840;Inherit;False;1666.333;632.2666;LatLong 
    Mapping;12;472;470;477;476;481;480;479;478;475;474;473;471;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;406;2688,2656;Inherit;False;181;276;UV;1;405;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;402;480,2656;Inherit;False;125;126.5;Dir;1;401;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;399;160,2000;Inherit;False;291.3333;284.6667;Amplify
    Shader Pack Example;1;371;;1,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;407;2688,3136;Inherit;False;181;276;DDX;1;408;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;409;2688,3424;Inherit;False;181;276;DDY;1;410;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;278;480,2000;Inherit;False;360.9391;129.989;;;0,0,0,1;UV
    LatLong Node converts a vector into UV coordinates for sampling a LatLong-formated
    texture.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0,
    Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;400;256,2592;Inherit;False;132.3918;100.5;Dir;;0,0,0,1;;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;423;672,2560;Inherit;False;360.9391;129.989;UV
    Lat Long Node;;0,0,0,1;UV LatLong Node converts a vector into UV coordinates
    for sampling a LatLong-formated texture.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;424;2080,2496;Inherit;False;537.4648;187.3208;;;0,0,0,1;Result
    (which is in radians) to UV coordinate range (0-1).$$Longitude for the texture
    is a full circle, or 2*Pi radians. Thus, the first constant is 1/(2*Pi) or about
    0.15915493. In the latitude, the span is half a circle, or Pi radians. The second
    constant would be 1/Pi or about 0.3183099, but it's premultiplied by -1 to save
    a multiplication step in the node graph.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;425;256,2816;Inherit;False;344.8912;160.7905;;;0,0,0,1;Common
    to create this vector as the reflection of the Camera Direction and the Normal
    Vector $$See $Reflection Node connected to the input.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;426;1360,3104;Inherit;False;277;123;;;0,0,0,1;The
    U coordinate of the projection is created using the arctangent2 of the X and
    Z components of the input vector and then adding PI/2.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;427;704,3168;Inherit;False;284;119;;;0,0,0,1;The
    V coordinate is calculated from the Y coordinate of the input vector.  We find
    the arccosine of that value and then add PI.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;428;2256,3008;Inherit;False;364.5;172.8;;;0,0,0,1;It's
    critical when using the UV coordinates generated by the UVLatLong node, that
    you set the Sample Texture 2D node to Gradient Mip Sampling Mode in the Inspector
    - and pass in the proper DDX, DDY derivatives as shown here.  Otherwise, you'll
    get an ugly seam on one side of the projection.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;429;2000,3024;Inherit;False;168.2363;100.5884;Invert
    Face;;0,0,0,1;value 0 = default$value 1 = Inverted;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.ATan2OpNode,
